James sought advice on adopting a cat to solve his persistent mouse problem, expressing frustration with traditional traps. I recommended various approaches to find a suitable cat, emphasizing local shelters, barn cat programs, and observing behavior for hunting instincts. I suggested focusing on young adult cats and the potential benefits of adopting in pairs. James also questioned if he should be explicit with the shelter about his mouse problem, expressing concern over being perceived as adopting for the wrong reasons. I reassured him that honesty is important, highlighting the value of transparency for matching with the right cat while reaffirming his commitment to care and companionship. This openness not only aids adoption but helps identify cats suited for pest control.
